  "analysis": [
    "display_text retains a nonempty, at-most-1024-UTF8-byte label. Unicode Cc characters are rejected except LF/TAB, matching Rust char::is_control exclusions. It independently retains the Rust finite display syntax prohibitions: hidden comments, wiki/image markers, HTML/autolink starts, Markdown link/reference tails and numeric-local-part email autolinks.",
    "The metadata exception requires an explicit identity_display_labels flag and the exact typed path (concepts, integer array index, display_name). Flags are passed only at v1/v2/v3 identity-map validation. Other nested objects, IDs, authors, context declarations and source candidate evidence retain their prior checks.",
    "All three coordination versions still apply exact schema fields, UUID checks, source reconstruction and original inventory protection. ID, filename and source-bundle validators were not changed by the patch.",
    "Presentation expected-schema changes only object/property label admission. The checker still binds those labels to reconstructed canonical concepts, reconstructs the full plan/Markdown/ranges/reports and compares originals; the new helper does not bypass complete verification.",
    "The added integration tests freeze unchanged source/atom gold and explicit label expectations before normal coordinate/present calls. They invoke complete coordination and presentation verifiers for versions 1, 2 and 3, and check protected original inventories after verification."
  ],
